This contains some spoilers, if you haven't guessed that already...

One of the things that's mentioned in the high-score file besides your
character's score is the number of hit points and max hit points that
the character died/ascended with. Often players don't just try for the
highest score, but also to get the most max hit points in the list.
Now with massive polypiling, cursed magic markers and scrolls, and
reverse genociding nurses, a character can (with difficulty) get up to
1000 hp or so, but this method is limited because of the limits on
scrolls, polymorph wands, etc. that can be found in the dungeon.
However, from some of the high score lists posted to the net, I've
seen that some people have gotten over ten thousand hit points! Now
the question is, how? The only (main) ways that one can up their max
number of hit points are:
	Gaining levels - (actually your max hit points will still go up even
			  when you reach level 30, although the level itself
			  will remain there. But there are relatively few
			  ways of gaining levels, e.g. killing monsters,
			  potions of gain level, etc.)
	Letting nurses hit you - (This is limited because of the number of
				  nurses that can be found and scrolls that
				  can be used to reverse genocide them.)
	Quaffing potions - (A blessed extra healing when you are at max will
			    up your max hp by 5 when quaffed; but again, this
			    is limited by the number of potions available.)
Obviously a scam to get mega hitpoints must take advantage of a loop
hole in one of these methods somewhere, and not rely on any objects
that can be exhausted.

The key spoilers:
	(a) If high charisma and/or experience, you can gain levels (and
	    increase max hp) by sleeping with a succubus.
	(b) An inexhaustible supply of succubi can be generated from
	    kicking a sink.

So what you do is:
	(1) Once your at a high level and have decent charisma, find a
	    level with a sink.
	(2) Kick the sink until you get a succubus (i.e. "The dishwasher
	    returns"). Note that you might also get a black pudding, so
	    be prepared for it, e.g. genocide them, kill enough of them
	    so they get auto-genocided, levitate over an Elbereth, or
	    rustproof all your stuff, etc. You might also find a ring
	    (though only once per sink). Don't quaff from the sink, unless
	    you want to risk polymorphing or having it turn into a fountain.
	(3) #chat with the succubus and let her take off all your armor,
	    and let "time stand still". You will generally "enjoy it more
	    than the succubus" and will sometimes "feel that that was a very
	    educational experience", in which case you will gain a level,
	    and 6 hit points to your maximum if already at level 30.
	(4) Once you finish with the succubus, she will have teleported to
	    another part of the level. At first she will "have a headache"
	    if you find her and #chat again, but after a while she will get
	    over it. Repeat the process and the level can soon be filled
	    with succubi!
(Note: This of course assumes that your character is male, because
otherwise you would have to find an incubus in order to be able to
"get laid" in the game. I don't know off hand when the "dishwasher
returns" if it will be an incubus if you are playing a female
character, but at least it will never be an incubus if your
character is male.)

So (no pun intended :-) you can get a really tough character by
spending your time screwing around. With this method one could get a
huge supply of hit points (and spell points too, because they increase
with your level) which would make your character almost immortal.

So, for all of us nethack abusers out there, we have three main scams:
(1) The invisible leprechaun stealing gold back from the temple priest and
    then re#chatting with it to get -127 intrinsic AC scam.
(2) The put stuff in blessed bag of holding and removing it after cursing it
    and then putting tons of rocks polymorphed into gems to get 10-100
    million points scam.
(3) The kick the sink and #chat with the succubus to get several thousand
    max hit points scam.

Of course although all of these work in pl10, none of them will
probably work in 3.1. But then, 3.1 won't be out for a while yet, and
we nethackers have to keep ourselves occupied in some way until then..

